cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below, together with the underlying sources listed under 'references'."
title: "NEXUS · HUD: A Self-Contained Offline Astronomical Ephemeris Engine"
abstract: >-
  NEXUS · HUD is a single-file HTML application providing high-precision
  ephemerides for the Sun, the Moon, and a curated catalogue of 80 bright
  stars, with interactive 3D visualisation of the celestial sphere and the
  lunar surface, a Besselian eclipse-path renderer with Watts limb
  correction, a GNSS-aware time-scale converter spanning 12 scales, and an
  embedded self-audit of 113 numerical checks executed live in the browser.
  The software has no external dependencies and requires no network access.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kawi"
    given-names: "Ra"
    alias: "rakawi182"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rakawi182/NEXUS-ESO18"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - ephemeris
  - celestial mechanics
  - lunar theory
  - eclipse prediction
  - time scales
  - GNSS
  - WebGL
  - offline application
